# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded 10^x - 1 of BF16
#
# For |x| < 2^-10 the Taylor expansion ln(10) x + (ln(10) x)^2/2 in B32. Otherwise x = x1 + x2, where x1 keeps the
# sign, the exponent and the upper 4 bits of the mantissa and x2 the exponent and the lower 3 bits:
# 10^x - 1 = 10^x1 10^x2 - 1, both factors tabulated as B32 values, combined with one fused multiply-add. Round to
# nearest only: overflow gives +inf, large negative x gives -1, NaN comes back quiet.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binaryb16/exp10m1/exp10m1_bf16.c.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/System/Numerics/BF16

